{"name":"Grey Linnet Egg","hex":"#f2e8d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"linnet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small passerine bird, the common linnet (Linaria cannabina syn. Carduelis cannabina), in the finch family Fringillidae, native to Europe, western Asia, and north Africa.","A house finch (Haemorhous mexicanus), of North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linnet"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common linnet","blocks":[{"text":"The common linnet or Eurasian linnet is a small passerine bird of the finch family, Fringillidae. It derives its common name and the scientific name, Linaria, from its fondness for hemp seeds and flax seeds—flax being the English name of the plant from which linen is made."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Carduelis_cannabina_-England_-male-8.jpg/330px-Carduelis_cannabina_-England_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_linnet","wikidata":"Q27075852"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg/500px-2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg/12